back from the dead with thoughts on her panini press.

177
00:07:28,120 --> 00:07:30,340
别在清醒时 一直打电话骚扰人家了
Stop sober dialing Martha Stewart!

178
00:07:30,400 --> 00:07:31,760
谁说我清醒了
Who says I'm sober?

179
00:07:32,460 --> 00:07:33,380
麦克斯 你的手机给我
Max, give me your phone.

180
00:07:36,743 --> 00:07:39,249
老娘的"奶"昔招蜂引蝶一流 *
* My milkshake brings all the boys to the yard.

181
00:07:40,200 --> 00:07:41,540
把我的手机换给我
Now give me my phone.

182
00:07:41,920 --> 00:07:43,040
拿去 行了吧
Okay, take it, done.

183
00:07:43,060 --> 00:07:43,700
我看开了
I'm over her.

184
00:07:45,020 --> 00:07:46,520
她什么时候才会打给我啊
When is she gonna call me?

185
00:07:46,620 --> 00:07:48,980
我的"奶"昔一定能把她招来的
My milkshake would totally bring her to the yard.

186
00:07:49,940 --> 00:07:51,700
麦克斯 这不像你啊
Max, this isn't you.

187
00:07:51,700 --> 00:07:53,000
你是女强人
I mean, you're strong.

188
00:07:53,080 --> 00:07:53,999
女硬汉
You're a badass.

189
00:07:53,999 --> 00:07:56,531
你吃止痛药就能消灭乳突病毒了
You beat H.P.V. with tylenol.

190
00:07:56,980 --> 00:07:58,900
而且你是吃的还是杂牌货
And it wasn't even the name brand.

191
00:07:59,720 --> 00:08:00,860
你这是怎么回事
What's wrong with you?

192
00:08:00,940 --> 00:08:02,840
玛莎破了我的处 行了吧
I was a virgin before Martha, okay?

193
00:08:03,140 --> 00:08:05,460
在她之前 从来没有人夸过我行
No one ever told me I was good at anything before her.

194
00:08:05,460 --> 00:08:07,460
人生"第一个"大款白女人哪能说忘就忘
And you never forget your first rich white woman.

195
00:08:08,300 --> 00:08:09,760
无论有没有她的帮忙
With or without Martha Stewart,

196
00:08:09,760 --> 00:08:11,320
我们都会建立起自己的小蛋糕生意
We're gonna build our cupcake business

197
00:08:11,320 --> 00:08:13,140
然后飞黄腾达 我看得见那未来
And be a success, I just know it.

198
00:08:13,240 --> 00:08:14,820
你怎么看得到 你怎么能肯定
How? How do you know that?

199
00:08:14,860 --> 00:08:16,820
那是因为我知道你有天赋
I know because you have the talent,

200
00:08:16,820 --> 00:08:18,940
我有洞察力 因为我能感觉到成功在望
I have the vision, and because I feel it.

201
00:08:19,120 --> 00:08:20,120
打从心里感觉到
I feel it here.

202
00:08:20,120 --> 00:08:22,420
恶心啊 还你的心呢
Oh, blegh! Your heart?

203
00:08:23,120 --> 00:08:25,900
不是啦 是我的幸运珍珠项链
No. My pearls- my lucky pearls.

204
00:08:26,520 --> 00:08:27,900
是幸运还是丑爆啊
By lucky, do you mean ugly?

205
00:08:28,600 --> 00:08:30,040
自从我被驱逐出我家之后
I've worn these every day

206
00:08:30,040 --> 00:08:31,720
我就天天戴着它
since I was evicted from my townhouse.

207
00:08:31,840 --> 00:08:33,540
这珍珠项链给我带来好运
This pearl necklace brings me luck.

208
00:08:34,370 --> 00:08:34,980
你...
You--

209
00:08:34,980 --> 00:08:36,920
你觉得你好运吗
You think your life is lucky?

210
00:08:37,740 --> 00:08:41,100
今早你用厕纸当咖啡机滤纸
This morning you used toilet paper as a coffee filter...

211
00:08:41,100 --> 00:08:43,960
滤完之后再拿回去当厕纸用
and then used it as toilet paper.

212
00:08:45,260 --> 00:08:47,340
我知道你觉得我白痴
I know this sounds silly to you,

213
00:08:47,340 --> 00:08:48,560
但每天我只要一戴上
But there is something about

214
00:08:48,560 --> 00:08:49,940
我的珍珠项链
putting on these pearls every day

215
00:08:49,940 --> 00:08:51,540
就会觉得自己既坚强又自信
that makes me feel strong, confident,

216
00:08:52,280 --> 00:08:53,900
好像一切皆有可能
and like anything is possible.

217
00:08:54,260 --> 00:08:55,920
而只要我还有幸运项链的陪...
And as long as I have these lucky--

218
00:09:00,360 --> 00:09:02,380
不是吧 不是吧
Oh, no. Oh, no!

219
00:09:02,623 --> 00:09:03,727
别别别 别恐慌
No, no, no, don't freak out.

220
00:09:03,940 --> 00:09:04,880
别恐慌 我们快捡回来
Don't freak out. We'll get em.

221
00:09:08,740 --> 00:09:09,700
我的珍珠
My pearls!

222
00:09:09,800 --> 00:09:10,780
我的幸运珍珠
My lucky pearls!

223
00:09:10,920 --> 00:09:13,200
是是是 我们知道有什么麻烦
Yes, yes, we have identified the problem.

224
00:09:13,220 --> 00:09:14,120
快动手捡起来吧
Just pick them up.

225
00:09:23,880 --> 00:09:25,398
看来有人先行享用早餐啦
Looks like somebody found breakfast.

226
00:09:25,398 --> 00:09:27,294
栗宝 不可以
No, chestnut!

227
00:09:28,840 --> 00:09:30,120
这锅我会继续拿来做哦
I'm still using that.

228
00:09:31,180 --> 00:09:32,960
现在做什么都是徒劳无功
Well, nothing's gonna work out now.

229
00:09:33,120 --> 00:09:34,100
厄运已经降临了
Here comes the bad luck.

230
00:09:34,480 --> 00:09:35,440
说什么傻话
Don't be ridiculous.

231
00:09:35,580 --> 00:09:37,340
你本来就衰到不能再衰了
Your luck couldn't get any worse.

232
00:09:46,500 --> 00:09:47,220
原来真的一切皆有可能
Or could it?

233
00:09:53,440 --> 00:09:54,317
你看 厄尔
Okay, Earl.

234
00:09:54,317 --> 00:09:57,820
这是L-520点菜系统触控板
This is the L-520 order system touch pad.

235
00:09:57,820 --> 00:09:59,600
你看有多简单 瞧
Look how simple. See?

236
00:10:00,100 --> 00:10:01,160
你听我说
I'm telling you,

237
00:10:01,160 --> 00:10:03,280
我学不会这复杂的玩意
I can't figure this tricky little thing out.

238
00:10:03,900 --> 00:10:05,740
厄尔 刚才的是开关钮
Earl, it's an on/off button.

239
00:10:06,100 --> 00:10:07,380
不会吧
Oh, slow down.

240
00:10:07,620 --> 00:10:08,740
那一键还两用啊
It does both?

241
00:10:10,940 --> 00:10:13,560
我先帮把这宝贝充上电吧
Let me just charge this up for you right here.

242
00:10:16,960 --> 00:10:18,080
这块插线板
This thing has been plugged

243
00:10:18,080 --> 00:10:19,600
比卡戴珊姐妹被"插"得还满啊
more than the Kardashian sisters.

244
00:10:22,039 --> 00:10:25,158
我还是先检查一下餐馆这老电路吧
I better check the old wiring in diner first.

245
00:10:25,780 --> 00:10:27,680
麦克斯 我现在感觉大家都在
Max, now I feel like everyone's staring

246
00:10:27,680 --> 00:10:28,740
盯着我胸口看
at my chest area.

247
00:10:29,080 --> 00:10:30,220
欢迎来到我的世界
Well, welcome to my life,

248
00:10:30,220 --> 00:10:31,300
我九岁之后就过着这样的生活
Every day since I was nine.

249
00:10:32,760 --> 00:10:34,820
那珍珠项链对我有特别意义
That necklace meant something special to me.

250
00:10:34,880 --> 00:10:36,720
难道你没有失去过你拥有很久
Didn't you ever lose anything sentimental

251
00:10:36,720 --> 00:10:38,040
感情深厚的事物吗
you had for a long time?

252
00:10:38,420 --> 00:10:40,440
我妈啊 不过后来她又自己跑回来了
My mother, but then she found her way back.

253
00:10:41,220 --> 00:10:43,680
我受够了一直等她回电
Look, I am done waiting for Martha to call.

254
00:10:44,060 --> 00:10:46,160
不如我们再做点蛋糕去找她
I say we go down there with some cupcakes,

255
00:10:46,180 --> 00:10:47,440
提醒她当初她有多喜欢它们
remind her how much she liked them,

256
00:10:47,460 --> 00:10:48,760
然后建议她邀请我们上她节目
and suggest she puts us on her show.

257
00:10:49,240 --> 00:10:51,540
不行 我珍珠都没了怎么去见人啊
No, I mean, I can't go without my pearls.

258
00:10:51,860 --> 00:10:53,520
它不仅仅代表着好运
And it's more than just the luck.

259
00:10:53,560 --> 00:10:55,760
还代表着我破产前的身份
It's who I was before I lost everything.

260
00:10:56,380 --> 00:10:57,480
你知道我说
You know how I always say,

261
00:10:57,740 --> 00:10:58,940
"你好 我是卡洛琳·钱宁"时
"Hi, I'm Caroline Channing,"

262
00:10:58,940 --> 00:11:00,120
每次都会摸摸珍珠吧
and then touch my pearls?

263
00:11:00,440 --> 00:11:01,960
我不只是在自我介绍
I'm not just introducing myself.

264
00:11:01,960 --> 00:11:03,340
那也是在提醒我自己
I'm reminding myself.

265
00:11:03,720 --> 00:11:05,880
那让我也提醒你另外一件事吧
Well, let me remind you of something else.

266
00:11:06,240 --> 00:11:07,340
昨天你告诉我
Yesterday you told me

267
00:11:07,340 --> 00:11:09,180
我们能靠着小蛋糕征服全世界呢
we were going to rule the world with cupcakes.

268
00:11:09,460 --> 00:11:10,780
有珍珠撑腰 说话自然气壮
Yeah, that was the pearls talking.

269
00:11:12,140 --> 00:11:13,500
那现在轮到我说了
Okay, well, now I'm talking.

270
00:11:13,820 --> 00:11:14,880
幸运是不存在的
There is no luck.

271
00:11:15,040 --> 00:11:16,100
努力才是硬道理
There is only work.

272
00:11:16,300 --> 00:11:18,480
可你现在只让我想对你使用暴"力"
And right now, you're working my last nerve.

273
00:11:18,480 --> 00:11:20,480
所以我打算自己去找她
So I am going down there myself.

274
00:11:20,480 --> 00:11:21,740
如果她不愿意帮忙
and if Martha won't help me,

275
00:11:22,380 --> 00:11:23,920
我就用擀面棍打爆她膝盖
I'ma bust her kneecaps with a rolling pin

276
00:11:23,920 --> 00:11:26,160
然后说"这样才是一件好事"
and then say, "now that's a good thing."

277
00:11:34,080 --> 00:11:36,140
这样吧 我们给她发封电邮如何
Okay, what if we just send Martha an E-mail,

278
00:11:36,360 --> 00:11:37,740
这样就不用去到她办公楼
so we're not just standing in her office,

279
00:11:37,740 --> 00:11:38,811
求前台放我们进去了
begging some receptionist?

280
00:11:38,811 --> 00:11:40,980
-那样一点屁用都没有 -有用的
- That won't do anything. - Yes, it will.

281
00:11:40,980 --> 00:11:42,080
我超会写商业电邮呢
I craft amazing business E-mails.

282
00:11:42,700 --> 00:11:43,340
我可是沃顿高材生呢
I went to Wharton.

283
00:11:43,600 --> 00:11:45,480
求你嘴下留情 我就剩这点资本了
Please don't, Max. That's all I have left.

284
00:11:46,960 --> 00:11:48,960
麦克斯 卡洛琳
Max, Caroline, I found something

285
00:11:48,960 --> 00:11:50,140
我在餐馆贸易展览里
at the restaurant trade show

286
00:11:50,140 --> 00:11:51,380
发现了点你们会感兴趣的东西哦
you might be interested in.

287
00:11:51,580 --> 00:11:53,380
我唯一有兴趣的餐馆贸易
The only restaurant trade I'm interested in

288
00:11:53,380 --> 00:11:55,760
就是看能不能把你以物易物走
is if we can exchange you for anybody else.

289
00:11:56,960 --> 00:11:58,680
看了你就不会笑我了
You won't be laughing in a minute.

290
00:11:59,160 --> 00:12:00,620
你看 这是我从最新研发的
Look, it's a cupcake from the new

291
00:12:00,620 --> 00:12:02,600
自助小蛋糕机买来的小蛋糕
state-of-the-art cupcake ATM machine.

292
00:12:02,980 --> 00:12:04,960
人家连锁小蛋糕店打算城里广设这机器
Sprinkles cupcakes plans to be put them everywhere.

293
00:12:04,960 --> 00:12:08,140
很快 大家只需按下按钮
Soon, everyone will be able to just push a button,

294
00:12:08,140 --> 00:12:10,280
无论白天黑夜 随时都能吃到小蛋糕
Day or night, and get the cupcake.

295
00:12:10,960 --> 00:12:12,960
所以我想说的是
So, I guess what I'm saying is,

296
00:12:12,960 --> 00:12:14,380
你们俩可能完了
You might be screwed.

297
00:12:17,080 --> 00:12:17,560
美味可口
Delicious...

298
00:12:18,700 --> 00:12:19,980
不用受气
And no attitude.

299
00:12:23,580 --> 00:12:25,160
坏运气接踵而至
well, more bad luck.

300
00:12:25,300 --> 00:12:26,220
我原本以为你在开玩笑
I thought you were kidding,

301
00:12:26,220 --> 00:12:27,920
但机器真的要取代人类了
but the machines are taking over.

302
00:12:27,980 --> 00:12:29,060
我们斗不过机器
We can't compete with that.

303
00:12:29,080 --> 00:12:30,580
我们的生意完蛋了 游戏结束
The business is done. Game over.

304
00:12:31,020 --> 00:12:33,040
天啊 你这种态度怎么在未来混啊
Man, you are never gonna make it in the future.

305
00:12:33,520 --> 00:12:35,300
人类就应该在此时奋起反击
This is where the humans fight.

306
00:12:35,660 --> 00:12:37,280
我们就应该在此时 向玛莎·斯图尔特示威
This is where we march down to Martha Stewart

307
00:12:37,280 --> 00:12:38,720
要求她帮我们大力宣传
and demand a damn blurb,

308
00:12:38,720 --> 00:12:40,280
这样我们才能跟机器斗
So we can compete with the machines...

309
00:12:40,580 --> 00:12:43,380
就像《终结者2:甜点的觉醒》
Just like in "Terminator 2: rise of the desserts."

310
00:12:44,700 --> 00:12:46,080
好吧 我们去找玛莎
Fine. Let's go see Martha.

311
00:12:46,160 --> 00:12:47,000
她是我们唯一的希望了
She's our only hope.

312
00:12:47,220 --> 00:12:48,320
我的幸运项链没了
My lucky necklace is gone.

313
00:12:48,320 --> 00:12:50,120
我们不能再坐等奇迹发生
We can no longer just wait for magic to happen.

314
00:12:50,700 --> 00:12:51,740
对了 谢谢你啊
Uh, thank you, by the way,

315
00:12:51,760 --> 00:12:54,100
从没告诉我 原本的计划是等天降鸿福
for never telling me that our former plan was magic.

316
00:12:57,640 --> 00:13:00,640
我们向玛莎重新介绍自己 和我们的小蛋糕
We'll just reintroduce ourselves and our cupcakes to Martha

317
00:13:00,640 --> 00:13:02,120
然后让她再次记住我们
and impress her all over again,

318
00:13:02,140 --> 00:13:03,660
虽然现在的我 戴着一条我讨厌的项链
Even though I'm wearing a necklace that I hate.

319
00:13:03,740 --> 00:13:05,600
这项链没个性 没活力 没光泽
It's limp, anemic, and lackluster.

320
00:13:05,820 --> 00:13:07,360
我脖子上戴着的彷佛是奥尔森姐妹
I have an Olsen twin around my neck.

321
00:13:08,540 --> 00:13:08,960
拿着
here.

322
00:13:09,800 --> 00:13:10,600
你这是干嘛
what are you doing?

323
00:13:11,320 --> 00:13:12,920
这样玛莎就能认出我了
so Martha will recognize me.

324
00:13:14,600 --> 00:13:16,480
打扰了 问你两件事
Hi, excuse me. Two questions.

325
00:13:16,560 --> 00:13:17,940
玛莎·斯图尔特的办公室在几楼
Which floor is Martha Stewart on?

326
00:13:17,940 --> 00:13:19,260
我应该拿掉这条项链吗
And should I lose this necklace?

327
00:13:20,840 --> 00:13:22,760
好吧 沉默说明一切
Well, your silence speaks volumes.

328
00:13:23,280 --> 00:13:24,860
你好 我不是疯子
Hi, I'm not crazy,

329
00:13:24,860 --> 00:13:26,260
你可以把楼层告诉我
so you can just tell me the floor number.

330
00:13:26,820 --> 00:13:28,360
15楼 电梯在那边
Elevator right over there, 15th floor,

331
00:13:28,440 --> 00:13:29,400
玛莎·斯图尔特生活媒体公司
Martha Stewart living omnimedia.

332
00:13:30,880 --> 00:13:32,240
有点小兴奋
Just got a little damp.

333
00:13:33,360 --> 00:13:35,400
谢谢你的建议 感觉好多了
Thanks for your help. Feels better.

334
00:13:36,140 --> 00:13:37,900
真聪明 问一个没有脖子的人
Smart, getting necklace advice

335
00:13:37,900 --> 00:13:38,860
你的脖子该不该戴项链
from a guy with no neck.

336
00:13:39,340 --> 00:13:41,520
慢着 那不就是...
Wait. Is that--

337
00:13:41,520 --> 00:13:43,819
那就是阿憨说的小蛋糕自助机
That's the cupcake machine that han was talking about.

338
00:13:43,819 --> 00:13:45,680
天啊
Ugh, no!

339
00:13:45,680 --> 00:13:47,080
我还希望它会很丑呢
I was hoping it'd be ugly,

340
00:13:47,080 --> 00:13:48,940
但它居然是粉色 而且很可爱
but it's pink and really cute.

341
00:13:49,180 --> 00:13:50,060
就像一台基佬版的R2-D2
It's like a gay R2-D2.

342
00:13:52,820 --> 00:13:54,340
R2-D2已经够基了 它更基一筹
Well, a gayer R2-D2.

343
00:13:55,780 --> 00:13:58,320
谁会想吃从这玩意出来的小蛋糕啊
Who wouldn't want a cupcake from this?

344
00:13:59,140 --> 00:14:00,020
没人
No one.

345
00:14:01,100 --> 00:14:02,580
-我们要给它点"颜色"看看 -什么
- We have to mess her up. - What?

346
00:14:02,780 --> 00:14:04,860
你怎么会在包里随身带着喷漆呢
Why are you carrying spray-paint in your purse?

347
00:14:05,120 --> 00:14:06,940
跟我随身带卫生棉条是一个道理
For the same reason I carry a tampon.

348
00:14:07,080 --> 00:14:08,020
以备不时之需嘛
'cause you never know.

349
00:14:08,580 --> 00:14:10,920
我们不能破坏人家的东西
We are not gonna destroy someone else's property.

350
00:14:11,500 --> 00:14:12,700
我们必需得做点什么啊
Well, we have to do something,

351
00:14:12,800 --> 00:14:14,020
我们不搞死它 它就会玩死我们
'cause it's that machine or us.

352
00:14:14,760 --> 00:14:15,640
我知道了
Oh, I know.

353
00:14:15,820 --> 00:14:17,920
我们可以打开那扇小门 放坨屎进去
We can open the little door and put a poop in it.

354
00:14:19,684 --> 00:14:21,040
当然不是我的啦 天啊
Not one of mine. Jeez!

355
00:14:21,040 --> 00:14:21,860
你把我当成什么了 猪吗
What am I, a pig?

356
00:14:23,220 --> 00:14:24,880
反正我是不干
Well, I'm not doing it.

357
00:14:25,620 --> 00:14:28,300
不是啦 我们可以从大街上捡点狗屎回来
No, we just get some puppy poop from the street.

358
00:14:28,980 --> 00:14:29,440
不要
No!

359
00:14:29,520 --> 00:14:31,240
我们没绝望到那种程度
We are not that desperate.

360
00:14:31,660 --> 00:14:32,420
而且我的湿巾纸用完了
And I'm out of wetnaps.

361
00:14:35,400 --> 00:14:37,160
不是的 我们以前跟玛莎见过面
No, see, we already met Martha.

362
00:14:37,260 --> 00:14:38,660
现在只是过来跟她问声好
We're just stopping by to say hi.

363
00:14:38,820 --> 00:14:40,240
你们以前跟玛莎见过面
You've already met Martha.

364
00:14:40,340 --> 00:14:42,700
-现在只是过来跟她问声好 -对
- You're just stopping by to say hi. - Yes.

365
00:14:43,000 --> 00:14:44,480
玛莎·斯图尔特要了我们的名片
Martha Stewart asked us for our card.

366
00:14:44,760 --> 00:14:46,800
玛莎·斯图尔特要了你们的名片
Martha Stewart asked you for your card.

367
00:14:47,480 --> 00:14:49,900
那我能问下玛莎在哪里要了你们的名片吗
And where should I tell Martha she asked for your card?

368
00:14:49,980 --> 00:14:50,780
女厕所
In the ladies' room.

369
00:14:51,600 --> 00:14:54,220
玛莎·斯图尔特在女厕所要了你们的名片
Martha Stewart asked you for your card in the ladies' room.

370
00:14:54,920 --> 00:14:55,280
好吧
Okay.

371
00:14:55,300 --> 00:14:57,120
别说得好像是我们瞎掰的 事实就是如此
Don't make it sound like that. It happened.

372
00:14:57,360 --> 00:14:58,580
我们在女厕所堵她 然后...
We cornered her in the ladies' room and--

373
00:14:58,700 --> 00:15:00,320
好了 也别说成是这样
okay, don't make it sound like that either.

374
00:15:00,840 --> 00:15:02,780
我们去晚会上碰运气
We went to a gala on the off chance

375
00:15:02,780 --> 00:15:03,860
希望玛莎能和蔼地尝一个
that she would be gracious enough

376
00:15:03,860 --> 00:15:05,340
我们做的小蛋糕 结果她的确尝了
to try one of our cupcakes and she did.

377
00:15:05,400 --> 00:15:06,400
她十分和蔼可亲
She was very gracious.

378
00:15:06,560 --> 00:15:08,300
对啊 或许"堵"这个词用得不太对
Yeah, maybe cornered was the wrong word.

379
00:15:08,380 --> 00:15:09,840
我们又不是去那里追捕她
It's not like we went there to hunt her down.

380
00:15:10,420 --> 00:15:12,380
你们又不是去那里追捕她
it's not like you went there to hunt her down.

381
00:15:13,460 --> 00:15:14,180
真的不是
It's not.

382
00:15:14,700 --> 00:15:16,340
好吧 我听出你的语气
Okay, I hear your tone.

383
00:15:16,480 --> 00:15:17,940
知道你的把戏是什么了
I see what's going down here.

384
00:15:17,940 --> 00:15:19,540
你觉得我们是来找麻烦的
You think I'm some kind of a problem.

385
00:15:19,640 --> 00:15:22,280
我要声明一句 是玛莎先撩我的
Well, for the record, Martha came on to me.

386
00:15:22,420 --> 00:15:23,980
好吧 算了
All right. Okay.

387
00:15:24,080 --> 00:15:26,120
此行不如我们预期般顺利
This is not going as well as we had hoped.

388
00:15:26,320 --> 00:15:28,700
没了我的魔法项链 果然一事无成
Don't know how it could without my magic pearls.

389
00:15:28,920 --> 00:15:29,700
好吧 听着
Okay, look.

390
00:15:29,700 --> 00:15:31,460
我明白你不会放我们进去
I get that you're not gonna let us up there.

391
00:15:31,460 --> 00:15:32,420
我也不怪你
And I don't blame you,

392
00:15:32,420 --> 00:15:34,360
因为这家伙在扯什么魔法
what, with this one talking about magic.

393
00:15:34,840 --> 00:15:36,560
但我得澄清 我们没有说谎
But just so you know, we are not lying.

394
00:15:36,720 --> 00:15:37,520
确有此事
It happened.

395
00:15:37,600 --> 00:15:38,880
在我们逮到她后
And after we hunted her down--

396
00:15:38,920 --> 00:15:40,460
没错 是你让我们不得不说出实话
Because, yeah, you got us on that, we did--

397
00:15:41,240 --> 00:15:42,400
玛莎对我们说
Martha told us

398
00:15:42,400 --> 00:15:44,720
她喜欢我们俩白手起家的精神
she liked our entrepreneurial drive.

399
00:15:45,860 --> 00:15:47,400
这话的确像是玛莎会说的
Well, that does sound like Martha.

400
00:15:48,180 --> 00:15:49,920
好吧 我帮你们送上去 先请坐吧
Okay, I'll send these up. Have a seat.

401
00:15:50,440 --> 00:15:52,200
太谢谢你了
Ahh, thank you so much.

402
00:15:52,440 --> 00:15:54,120
给 你拿一个试试吧
And here, uh, please take one,

403
00:15:54,120 --> 00:15:55,400
这样你也能亲自验证下
Just so you can see for yourself

404
00:15:55,400 --> 00:15:56,740
为什么玛莎会要我们的名片
why Martha asked for our card.

405
00:15:57,280 --> 00:15:58,660
好吧 我本来也打算等会
Well, I was gonna get a cupcake

406
00:15:58,660 --> 00:16:00,380
去楼下机器弄个小蛋糕吃
from that cute machine downstairs later.

407
00:16:00,480 --> 00:16:01,040
千万别去
Oh, don't.

408
00:16:01,240 --> 00:16:03,180
我听说 "一个小时后"有人会在里面
I heard someone found something nasty in that...

409
00:16:03,180 --> 00:16:03,931
发现怪东西呢
in about an hour.

410
00:16:03,931 --> 00:16:05,518
麦克斯
Max.

411
00:16:05,600 --> 00:16:07,120
这是我们的酒混面粉
And this is our beer batter

412
00:16:07,120 --> 00:16:08,940
加枫蜜培根的特制春假小蛋糕
Maple bacon spring break cupcake.

413
00:16:11,091 --> 00:16:13,900
我知道为什么玛莎会...
I can see why Martha-ow!

414
00:16:13,900 --> 00:16:14,380
什么
What the--

415
00:16:15,020 --> 00:16:16,440
我牙齿裂了
I cracked my tooth!

416
00:16:17,340 --> 00:16:18,440
什么
What? Oh!

417
00:16:18,440 --> 00:16:20,280
什么东西啊 是
What is that? Is it--

418
00:16:20,280 --> 00:16:21,500
是玻璃吗
Is that glass?

419
00:16:21,500 --> 00:16:22,800
不是 是珍珠
No, it's a pearl.

420
00:16:23,200 --> 00:16:24,620
真抱歉
I'm so sorry.

421
00:16:24,980 --> 00:16:26,620
抱歉 抱歉有屁用
Sorry? You're sorry?

422
00:16:27,220 --> 00:16:29,980
我都戴了11个月的透明矫正器了
I've been wearing invisaligns for 11 months!

423
00:16:32,540 --> 00:16:34,574
我们生意的大突破就此告终
Well, there goes our big break.

424
00:16:34,574 --> 00:16:37,440
如果我的幸运项链在的话 就不会发生这种事了
Never would've happened if I had had my necklace.

425
00:16:37,440 --> 00:16:38,640
你说的是那条有着幸运珍珠
The one with the lucky pearls

426
00:16:38,640 --> 00:16:40,240
结果线断珍珠撒 还掉进面粉糊里
that broke into the batter and that woman

427
00:16:40,240 --> 00:16:42,540
害人家口破血流口水滴的项链吗
just spit into her hand mixed with saliva and blood?

428
00:16:42,600 --> 00:16:43,480
是那条幸运项链吧
That lucky necklace?

429
00:16:45,140 --> 00:16:45,640
对啊
Yes.

430
00:16:47,000 --> 00:16:48,380
借此面对现实吧
Might as well face it.

431
00:16:48,380 --> 00:16:49,720
我们俩只能自食其力
You and I are on our own.

432
00:16:49,860 --> 00:16:51,340
这不只是因为玛莎的这件事
And not just because of Martha either.

433
00:16:51,400 --> 00:16:53,900
而是因为这世上没有所谓的"好运"
Because there is no such thing as good luck.

434
00:16:54,080 --> 00:16:54,940
见都没见过
Never seen it.

435
00:16:54,960 --> 00:16:57,160
所有的幸运物都愚蠢无比
And all lucky charms are stupid,

436
00:16:57,360 --> 00:16:59,100
唯一的例外是"幸运物早餐片"
except for the Lucky Charms,

437
00:16:59,180 --> 00:17:00,460
它奇迹般地好吃
which are magically delicious.

438
00:17:04,340 --> 00:17:05,920
看那台自助小蛋糕机
Look at it over there.

439
00:17:06,080 --> 00:17:08,460
基佬R2-D2都在笑我们了
Gay R2-D2 just laughing at us.

440
00:17:08,460 --> 00:17:09,640
麦克斯 你之前说得对
You were right, Max.

441
00:17:09,680 --> 00:17:10,780
我们俩只能自食其力了
You and I are on our own.

442
00:17:11,260 --> 00:17:12,940
我们只是一家刚起步的小蛋糕店
We're just a little start-up cupcake company

443
00:17:12,940 --> 00:17:14,700
在这乱世中求生存
in a hard, hard world.

444
00:17:14,700 --> 00:17:16,680
我们得亲自动手 扫除面前障碍
And we gotta take matters into our own hands.

445
00:17:17,380 --> 00:17:17,856
掩护我
Cover me.

446
00:17:17,856 --> 00:17:19,389
等等 别啊
Wait, wait, no.

447
00:17:19,880 --> 00:17:20,980
别现在干啊
No, don't do it now.

448
00:17:21,080 --> 00:17:22,800
-警卫就在那里呢 -喂 你
- The guard is right there. - Hey, you!

449
00:17:22,800 --> 00:17:23,540
快住手
Stop that!

450
00:17:23,940 --> 00:17:25,900
怎么会有变态想要乱喷小蛋糕机啊
What kind of freaks deface a cupcake machine?

451
00:17:25,940 --> 00:17:26,620
快跑快跑
Run run run.

452
00:17:30,100 --> 00:17:31,780
行了 停停停 甩掉他了
Okay, stop, stop, stop. We lost him.

453
00:17:33,440 --> 00:17:35,280
你知道你没喷到机器 只喷到了墙吧
You know you only tagged the wall, right?

454
00:17:35,660 --> 00:17:37,240
知道啊 我真是倒霉透了
Yes, I have no luck.

455
00:17:37,840 --> 00:17:39,680
世上没人有好运气
No one has any luck...

456
00:17:40,020 --> 00:17:42,520
除了林赛·罗韩的律师吧 有她这个回头客
with the possible exception of Lindsay Lohan's lawyer.

457
00:17:44,760 --> 00:17:45,720
你看 玛莎在那里
Look, it's Martha!

458
00:17:46,100 --> 00:17:47,940
她要上车了 把小蛋糕递给我
She's getting in that car. Give me the cupcakes.

459
00:17:48,060 --> 00:17:49,460
我要在那个吃到珍珠的女人
I'm going after her before she talks

460
00:17:49,460 --> 00:17:50,640
告状之前先跟她谈谈
to that lady whose mouth we broke.

461
00:17:52,340 --> 00:17:55,280
-麦克斯 别晃坏了小蛋糕 -别担心
- Max, don't jiggle the cupcakes! - Don't worry.

462
00:17:58,460 --> 00:18:01,021
老天啊 上帝啊 耶稣啊
Oh, my god. Oh, my god. Oh, my god.

463
00:18:01,021 --> 00:18:02,217
麦克斯 你没事吧
Max, are you all right?

464
00:18:02,217 --> 00:18:03,255
你还好吧
Are you all right?

465
00:18:03,880 --> 00:18:04,660
我没事
I'm fine.

466
00:18:05,980 --> 00:18:07,280
也没骨折
No broken bones,

467
00:18:07,680 --> 00:18:09,520
真是奇迹啊 因为我小时候
which is surprising, because when I was kid,

468
00:18:09,520 --> 00:18:10,440
没钱喝过牛奶补钙
we couldn't afford milk.

469
00:18:11,380 --> 00:18:13,060
我妈唯一买过一次牛奶
Actually the only time my mother bought milk

470
00:18:13,060 --> 00:18:14,693
还是因为牛奶盒上有我的照片呢[失踪儿童]
was when my face was on the side of the carton.

471
00:18:14,693 --> 00:18:17,204
你确定你真的没事吗
Are you sure you're all right?

472
00:18:17,660 --> 00:18:18,100
没事啦
Yeah.

473
00:18:18,940 --> 00:18:20,680
原来世上真的有幸运这么一件事
I guess there is such a thing as luck.

474
00:18:25,000 --> 00:18:26,320
从明晚开始
And tomorrow night

475
00:18:26,340 --> 00:18:27,920
当你再次步入餐厅呢 苏菲
when you come in for takeout, Sophie,

476
00:18:28,300 --> 00:18:30,400
麦克斯只需要轻击这个小东西
All Max has to do is hit this little thing.

477
00:18:30,400 --> 00:18:32,440
如果我可以这么做的话
Well, if I'm allowed to hit little things,

478
00:18:32,500 --> 00:18:33,180
我一定击爆你这个小东西
You're next.

479
00:18:34,260 --> 00:18:36,260
改变令大家都紧张兮兮
Change makes everyone so tense.

480
00:18:39,880 --> 00:18:40,820
厨房现在关了
Kitchen is now closed.

481
00:18:41,180 --> 00:18:42,160
我还有约
I have plans.

482
00:18:43,740 --> 00:18:44,700
重要的约呢
Big plans.

483
00:18:49,280 --> 00:18:51,120
苏菲 我知道
Sophie, I understand

484
00:18:51,120 --> 00:18:52,860
你跟奥列格的关系很复杂
your relationship with Oleg is complicated,

485
00:18:52,860 --> 00:18:54,060
所以我就简单一问
So let's simplify it.

486
00:18:54,220 --> 00:18:55,620
你今晚会在咱楼里做爱吗
Are you having sex in our building tonight,

487
00:18:55,620 --> 00:18:56,920
我需要先戴好耳塞吗
and do I have to wear earplugs?

488
00:18:57,680 --> 00:18:59,220
今晚我独守空闺
I will be alone...

489
00:18:59,880 --> 00:19:01,080
你还是戴着以防万一吧
But wear them anyway.

490
00:19:04,660 --> 00:19:06,480
您好 抱歉 我们关门了
Hi, um, sorry, we're closed.

491
00:19:06,560 --> 00:19:07,600
我不是来吃东西的
I do not wish to eat.

492
00:19:07,700 --> 00:19:09,420
奥列格打电话让我上门
I just got collect call from Oleg.

493
00:19:11,760 --> 00:19:13,960
她说关门了
She said we are closed.

494
00:19:14,880 --> 00:19:16,640
是吗 你哪位啊
Oh? And who are you?

495
00:19:16,980 --> 00:19:19,020
我是你被人废了双腿之前
I'm the last person you will see

496
00:19:19,020 --> 00:19:20,940
见到的最后那个人
before you learn how to walk again.

497
00:19:23,940 --> 00:19:25,798
离奥列格远点
Stay away from Oleg,

498
00:19:25,798 --> 00:19:28,880
不然老娘会把你的肠子从鼻孔拉出
Or I'll pull your intestines out through your nose

499
00:19:28,880 --> 00:19:31,640
然后送给她 当新项链戴
and give them to her to wear as new necklace.

500
00:19:33,180 --> 00:19:33,700
行
Fine.

501
00:19:34,160 --> 00:19:35,180
我走
I will leave.

502
00:19:35,480 --> 00:19:37,179
但我是给你蟒蛇般煞气的双眼面子
But only because you have eyes of a python,

503
00:19:37,179 --> 00:19:40,002
还有我最近貌似尿道感染了
And I have possible U.T.I.

504
00:19:42,600 --> 00:19:43,120
苏菲
Sophie...

505
00:19:43,880 --> 00:19:46,260
你就承认你跟奥列格关系不一般嘛
Why don't you just admit it, you and Oleg?

506
00:19:47,080 --> 00:19:47,600
什么
What?

507
00:19:48,120 --> 00:19:49,800
不是我想要他
It's not like I want him.

508
00:19:50,000 --> 00:19:51,940
只是我家乡那里的习惯是
It's just that where I come from,

509
00:19:51,940 --> 00:19:53,540
我用完了 也绝对不扔
You never throw anything away.

510
00:19:55,056 --> 00:19:57,235
拿去吧 姑娘们
Here you go, ladies.

511
00:19:57,660 --> 00:19:59,960
享受从刷卡的客人身上捞来额外小费吧
Enjoy the extra tips from your credit cards,

512
00:20:00,321 --> 00:20:02,700
因为阿憨一旦按下那个改朝换代的按钮
because when Han flips that switch,

513
00:20:02,700 --> 00:20:04,540
我能给你们的小费[小秘诀]
The only tip I can give you is,

514
00:20:04,540 --> 00:20:06,500
就只剩别天天洗头发了
don't wash your hair every day.

515
00:20:06,640 --> 00:20:07,640
头发会丧失水分的
It dries it out.

516
00:20:09,040 --> 00:20:11,520
好啦 一起迈向未来吧
Okay. Here comes the future.

517
00:20:12,240 --> 00:20:13,960
一 二
One, two--

518
00:20:18,340 --> 00:20:21,028
这破楼真他妈要把我搞死了
This old building sucks me so hard.

519
00:20:22,860 --> 00:20:24,060
恭喜你们俩啦
Congratulations, ladies.

520
00:20:24,060 --> 00:20:25,640
今晚是你们的幸运夜
This is your lucky night.

521
00:20:27,000 --> 00:20:28,300
说到幸运
Speaking of luck,

522
00:20:28,300 --> 00:20:30,060
这些是你的珍珠
here are your pearls.

523
00:20:30,740 --> 00:20:32,060
我找回了绝大多数
I found most of them, but I think

524
00:20:32,060 --> 00:20:33,000
但我猜栗宝吃掉了几颗
Chestnut ate a few.

525
00:20:33,220 --> 00:20:34,720
你之后自己去慢慢"挖掘"吧
You can dig for those later yourself.

526
00:20:35,146 --> 00:20:35,880
麦克斯
Max.

527
00:20:35,880 --> 00:20:37,700
但它是弄回不了原样了
And it won't look the same,

528
00:20:37,700 --> 00:20:39,900
因为你得自己用这便宜烂线穿上
because you have to string them on this cheap-ass wire

529
00:20:39,900 --> 00:20:41,580
这是我在嬉皮串珠店买的
I got at the hipster bead store...

530
00:20:41,580 --> 00:20:42,960
店名叫"得以珠之"
Beading off.

531
00:20:45,120 --> 00:20:46,500
我们可以把厄尔给我们的额外收入
We can add this Earl bonus money

532
